  "answer": "This feature request has been made before. PowerToys#150 ('Improved file tagging system') is the main tracking issue for file and folder tagging in Explorer, in the style of macOS tags. Other tagging requests were closed as duplicates of it, including #18039 and #40123. Nothing in those tickets says it has been built. Add a 👍 to #150 and put your OpenMeta cross-platform standard and AI-tagging ideas there. The tickets point to some existing third-party tools: FileMeta, Files, and Folder Marker. Commenters also noted that tags stored inside the file depend on the file format supporting them."
